{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"getSigit.siGitCode","latestVersion":"1.7.9","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Copyright 2026 PT Sigit Mitra Bangun","description":"siGit Code, an AI coding agent that runs on your machine.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Readme","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/getsigit/sigit/blob/main/README.md"}],"license":"Apache-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/getsigit/sigit/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Copyright 2026 PT Sigit Mitra Bangun","description":"siGit Code, an AI coding agent that runs on your machine.","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Readme","DocumentUrl":"https://github.com/getsigit/sigit/blob/main/README.md"}],"license":"Apache-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/getsigit/sigit/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"siGit Code is a local coding agent. It runs on your machine, not someone\nelse's. No API keys, no cloud round-trips, no subscription.\n\nIt works two ways from the same binary. Zed and other ACP-compatible\neditors start it over stdio and talk the Agent Client Protocol to it. Run\nit from a terminal and you get an interactive chat UI instead. On Windows\nit speaks ACP; the full-screen terminal UI is Unix-only.\n\nInference runs on-device against a GGUF model, or against siGit Code Cloud\nor any OpenAI-compatible endpoint you point it at.","moniker":"sigit","name":"siGit Code","packageUrl":"https://sigit.si/code","publisher":"getSigit","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/getsigit/sigit/issues","publisherUrl":"https://sigit.si/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/getsigit/sigit/releases/tag/v1.7.9","tags":["acp","agent","ai","cli","coding-agent","developer-tools","llm","terminal"]}},"longDescription":"siGit Code is a local coding agent. It runs on your machine, not someone\nelse's. No API keys, no cloud round-trips, no subscription.\n\nIt works two ways from the same binary. Zed and other ACP-compatible